# Code owners for discretus.
#
# The forge reads this file to decide who is requested for review when a pull
# request touches a path. The last matching pattern wins, so the general
# patterns come first and the specific ones come after, which is the opposite
# of how a reader might expect a configuration file to be ordered.
#
# What this file does and does not do:
#
#   It requests a review automatically. It does not block a merge on its own;
#   that is a branch protection setting.
#   It names an owner per path. It does not assign the work, and an owner who
#   is requested may reassign or decline.
#   It applies to the default branch. A change to this file takes effect for
#   pull requests opened after it merges.
#
# Syntax notes, because the pattern language is not quite the one used by
# .gitignore:
#
#   A pattern without a slash matches at any depth, so `*.py` matches every
#   Python file in the repository.
#   A pattern ending in a slash matches a directory and everything under it.
#   A leading slash anchors the pattern at the repository root.
#   A line with a path and no owner removes ownership for that path, which is
#   how an exception to a broader rule is expressed.
#
# The project currently has one maintainer, so every rule below names the same
# person. The file is nonetheless written with the structure it will need when
# there are domain reviewers, because the alternative is a single wildcard
# line that has to be rewritten from scratch the first time somebody else
# reviews. AUTHORS.md lists the roles that are open, and a contributor who
# reviews well within one domain over several pull requests will be invited to
# hold the corresponding role, at which point their entry is added here.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Default owner
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Everything not matched by a later rule.
*                                   @olaflaitinen

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The core layer
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A change here affects every domain package, because the core defines what an
# element is, what a relation and a function are, how exact arithmetic
# behaves, and how a structure verifies its axioms. It is reviewed more
# strictly than a change confined to one domain, and it is the one area where
# a second opinion will be sought first once a second reviewer exists.
/discretus/core/                    @olaflaitinen
/discretus/exceptions.py            @olaflaitinen
/discretus/errors.py                @olaflaitinen
/discretus/typing.py                @olaflaitinen
/discretus/protocols.py             @olaflaitinen
